WEBVTT

00:08.980 --> 00:11.202
I can see my house from here.

00:11.210 --> 00:13.282
I'm nothing but an insignificant ant...

00:13.290 --> 00:15.312
U-tan, Kuma-chan!

00:15.320 --> 00:17.700
Let's get to practicing!

00:20.280 --> 00:22.490
Your home is incredible.

00:23.640 --> 00:26.330
See? This is why I didn't
want you girls here.

00:26.670 --> 00:29.152
Huh? How come? You live in an awesome place.

00:29.160 --> 00:33.530
That's the thing. My home's
impressive while I'm like this.

00:34.120 --> 00:35.150
Like what?

00:35.960 --> 00:37.740
How do I put it?

00:38.410 --> 00:42.180
Everyone in my family's
outstanding except me.

00:43.110 --> 00:45.802
My parents are successful designers.

00:45.810 --> 00:48.810
My older brother and sister
have always been brilliant.

00:49.370 --> 00:51.980
No surprise they landed
themselves admirable jobs.

00:52.380 --> 00:54.390
All of them are winning in life.

00:54.920 --> 00:58.922
Meanwhile there's me,
unremarkable in every possible way.

00:58.930 --> 01:02.440
Bleaching my hair was a last ditch attempt
at giving myself some kind of trait.

01:03.140 --> 01:04.562
That's not true.

01:04.570 --> 01:06.202
It so is.

01:06.210 --> 01:09.232
Despite that, I'm quick
to get into whatever seems cool

01:09.240 --> 01:13.752
and have my folks buy me stuff,
only to lose interest just as fast.

01:13.760 --> 01:15.580
Talk about commitment issues.

01:15.900 --> 01:20.102
The worst part is I'm pretty decent
at whatever I get into at the start.

01:20.110 --> 01:21.452
Same thing with vocal percussion.

01:21.460 --> 01:23.732
I'm just not good
at repeating basic practice,

01:23.740 --> 01:25.840
and then I hit a wall and get fed up.

01:26.270 --> 01:32.360
It's because I'm like this that I don't have
any dreams or goals like everyone else.

01:33.990 --> 01:37.462
Maybe that's why I butt heads
with people like Omusubi

01:37.470 --> 01:40.932
who have a one-track mind
towards their dream.

01:40.940 --> 01:42.730
Do I have a inferiority complex?

01:43.700 --> 01:46.500
Wasn't being a MeTuber your dream?

01:47.220 --> 01:48.902
I'm not so sure.

01:48.910 --> 01:50.312
I couldn't think of anything else

01:50.320 --> 01:54.102
that could give me a sudden claim
to fame with little effort.

01:54.110 --> 01:57.302
I can't even tell if I genuinely
want to be one.

01:57.310 --> 02:02.012
Guess I wanted to do something?
Anything's better than nothing...

02:02.020 --> 02:06.750
I totally get it... you'll expose your
lack of confidence otherwise...

02:07.370 --> 02:09.872
Yeah, that might be it.

02:09.880 --> 02:12.600
I can't take people seeing the real me.

02:16.710 --> 02:19.052
Whoa, easy on the doom and gloom.

02:19.060 --> 02:22.952
Sorry 'bout that. I never talked about
myself so personally before,

02:22.960 --> 02:24.570
so things kinda took a serious turn.

02:25.260 --> 02:29.430
Then why did you bring up
practicing together at home?

02:29.860 --> 02:31.962
Yeah, about that...

02:31.970 --> 02:35.270
You know how Kuma-chan and I
have been working our butts off lately?

02:36.520 --> 02:38.360
Vocal percussion's super tricky.

02:38.820 --> 02:42.730
Feels like I can't keep up
now that I'm going at it for real.

02:44.330 --> 02:47.582
Meanwhile, Kuma-chan here's
stumbling every step of the way.

02:47.590 --> 02:50.812
I can totes tell from all our time together.

02:50.820 --> 02:54.312
You're right... I'm also having
trouble memorizing things...

02:54.320 --> 02:59.850
Despite that, the way she keeps
trucking on is honestly awe-inspiring.

03:00.670 --> 03:03.670
She makes me think that it's
also cool to be uncool.

03:06.750 --> 03:12.870
So now I want to put in the work, even if it
means fumbling and embarrassing myself.

03:14.010 --> 03:17.060
I'm trying to change, step by step.

03:18.680 --> 03:21.462
Sorry! Making it all about me was lame!

03:21.470 --> 03:22.180
You're cool!

03:23.850 --> 03:25.620
Ururu-chan, you're cool!

03:29.400 --> 03:31.980
Sharing stuff about myself's pretty wicked.

03:46.410 --> 03:52.170
"Harmony of Mille-Feuille"

05:02.480 --> 05:07.310
"Harmony of Mille-Feuille"

05:22.150 --> 05:22.700
Oh?

05:25.390 --> 05:26.580
What's wrong?

05:27.230 --> 05:28.292
President!

05:28.300 --> 05:29.290
Did something happen?

05:29.550 --> 05:32.482
Get a load of this, Airi-san!

05:32.490 --> 05:35.420
We're getting worse the more we try!

05:36.940 --> 05:39.760
It never felt like this
whenever we all sang together.

05:40.260 --> 05:45.322
But with just the three of us,
getting the tune right seems harder.

05:45.330 --> 05:47.412
Like we're out of sync.

05:47.420 --> 05:48.600
I see.

05:48.880 --> 05:54.480
Thinking about it, it's difficult to sing
with only the percussion and bass.

05:54.770 --> 05:56.032
I know what you mean.

05:56.040 --> 05:58.732
It's easy to take in someone singing a song,

05:58.740 --> 06:01.110
but vocal percussion
and bass are another matter.

06:01.500 --> 06:03.780
Yeah, that's exactly it.

06:04.210 --> 06:07.702
Since there's no issue singing as a band,

06:07.710 --> 06:10.630
I'd say it's good enough
to keep things as is.

06:11.250 --> 06:13.490
Is it really?

06:14.230 --> 06:20.102
Frankly, I don't think we really tried to
work with Ururu and Kuma-chan's rhythm.

06:20.110 --> 06:21.072
Reirei?

06:21.080 --> 06:23.340
What does that mean?

06:23.840 --> 06:26.982
So, remember how we said
a cappella rightfully involves

06:26.990 --> 06:30.932
controlling the rhythm via
the vocal percussion and bass?

06:30.940 --> 06:33.582
Yes, the rhythm section is key.

06:33.590 --> 06:40.390
The way I see it, we've been pacing
ourselves instead of turning to your rhythm.

06:40.810 --> 06:47.442
You mean everyone was following
their separate rhythms instead of ours?

06:47.450 --> 06:50.650
Is it because our rhythm
is all over the place?

06:51.610 --> 06:52.650
That would be the case.

06:54.270 --> 06:58.450
The person who's been in control
of the band's rhythm... is Musubu.

07:00.450 --> 07:05.312
I suspect Uta-chan's been unconsciously
turning to Musubu's rhythm.

07:05.320 --> 07:08.102
That's why she struggles to sing
alongside the rhythm section.

07:08.110 --> 07:10.420
I think you're right.

07:10.830 --> 07:13.482
You're both still new to this.

07:13.490 --> 07:19.090
There's nothing wrong with letting
the chorus redirect the rhythm.

07:19.800 --> 07:22.372
Wouldn't that lead to a repeat of our recital

07:22.380 --> 07:26.050
where everything fell apart
once I fumbled massively?

07:26.450 --> 07:27.302
Well...

07:27.310 --> 07:28.220
It would.

07:29.220 --> 07:30.640
Then this has to stop now!

07:32.090 --> 07:35.692
I want you to leave the rhythm
entirely to Kuma-chan and me!

07:35.700 --> 07:37.142
Let us hold the reins!

07:37.150 --> 07:38.980
I'd like that, too.

07:39.410 --> 07:42.900
I want to support everyone
with our own rhythm.

07:43.270 --> 07:45.912
It's not going to be easy.

07:45.920 --> 07:46.602
I know.

07:46.610 --> 07:50.052
The quality of our performances
will drop at the beginning.

07:50.060 --> 07:50.662
Will you-

07:50.670 --> 07:53.740
We'll bring it back up
by the school festival.

07:54.570 --> 07:55.370
Let's do this.

07:58.040 --> 08:03.522
This time, I want to get what Airi-san
taught me right without giving up.

08:03.530 --> 08:06.202
That's the kind of a cappella
I want to sing as well.

08:06.210 --> 08:09.652
I want to show we're just as good without
Musubu-chan doing all the heavy lifting.

08:09.660 --> 08:10.510
Me too.

08:12.140 --> 08:14.970
Alright, we'll do just that.

08:16.110 --> 08:17.930
-Thanks!
-Thank you!

08:21.090 --> 08:23.132
Was that the right choice?

08:23.140 --> 08:26.982
It's fine as long as it's
the performance they want.

08:26.990 --> 08:30.400
The three of them are capable
of singing a cappella on their own now.

08:30.980 --> 08:35.640
Why can't I be happy at
how everyone's changing?

08:36.130 --> 08:39.400
It was you who triggered these changes.

08:43.970 --> 08:46.960
Why don't you try changing yourself then?

08:48.510 --> 08:50.912
I'm unable to change...

08:50.920 --> 08:53.332
Let's try this part again.

08:53.340 --> 08:53.840
Okay.

09:04.780 --> 09:09.762
Um, I wish to eat my bread.
May I be permitted to dine here?

09:09.770 --> 09:11.652
I don't own the rooftop.

09:11.660 --> 09:13.752
Oh, you do.

09:13.760 --> 09:15.690
Yeah, right.

09:23.710 --> 09:24.610
I'm sorry!

09:24.900 --> 09:25.812
For what?

09:25.820 --> 09:29.242
I thought I may have
bothered you with my noise.

09:29.250 --> 09:32.440
I'm more bothered by how you have
crumbs all over you.

09:35.370 --> 09:37.462
So, how's practice?

09:37.470 --> 09:38.660
Perfect.

09:39.470 --> 09:42.742
Wow... guess I shouldn't expect
any less from you.

09:42.750 --> 09:44.232
How's yours?

09:44.240 --> 09:47.682
Um, a lot of things went down,
but we're good.

09:47.690 --> 09:48.760
It's been fun.

09:49.130 --> 09:51.590
Sure... fun, huh?

09:53.700 --> 09:59.052
So um, Musubu-chan,
won't you practice with us?

09:59.060 --> 10:00.140
Nope.

10:01.390 --> 10:03.130
I don't want to get all pissy.

10:03.670 --> 10:05.260
Okay, I understand.

10:05.660 --> 10:10.260
I'm just happy that you never
quit the club despite that.

10:12.010 --> 10:13.780
We can still sing a cappella together.

10:15.820 --> 10:16.700
Sorry...

10:17.010 --> 10:19.352
Eh? S-Sorry for that?

10:19.360 --> 10:22.052
I know that I'm the weirdo here.

10:22.060 --> 10:26.432
I'm not the kind of person
who's fit for these club activities.

10:26.440 --> 10:27.722
That's not-

10:27.730 --> 10:30.490
I really ought to have quit, except...

10:30.890 --> 10:33.012
My mom told me to continue.

10:33.020 --> 10:36.960
Your mom? Isn't she a professional singer?

10:37.350 --> 10:40.930
Yeah... she's who I admire and want to be...

10:41.340 --> 10:46.672
My mom's indecipherable, and now she
wants me to stay in the a cappella club.

10:46.680 --> 10:48.510
I don't get her at all.

10:48.970 --> 10:55.392
Back in middle school, I was in
the choir club. Because Mom said so.

10:55.400 --> 10:57.962
I was all fired up to meet her expectations.

10:57.970 --> 10:59.360
I see.

10:59.740 --> 11:04.000
Instead I destroyed the club holding
everyone up to my own standards.

11:04.970 --> 11:07.312
It's not like I wanted to wreck it.

11:07.320 --> 11:10.802
But I refuse to compromise
when it comes to music.

11:10.810 --> 11:13.240
I hate putting out the wrong note.

11:13.650 --> 11:16.200
That's the kind of being I am.

11:18.010 --> 11:21.062
Relax, I'm not gonna quit.

11:21.070 --> 11:25.940
It seems that whatever I need to
become a singer can be found in the club.

11:26.660 --> 11:28.522
Not that I can picture what it is.

11:28.530 --> 11:32.582
I think I have a bit of an idea
what your mom's thinking.

11:32.590 --> 11:33.300
Huh?

11:33.900 --> 11:36.562
Can you not say things you don't even mean?

11:36.570 --> 11:38.670
How the hell would you know?

11:41.130 --> 11:45.400
Of course I would. Like her,
I want you to enjoy being in the club.

11:47.090 --> 11:52.912
Like what I texted before, you're
not the kind of person who'd be in a club.

11:52.920 --> 11:57.740
But the fact is you're in front of me,
and we're singing a cappella!

11:58.190 --> 12:00.280
I want to make to so you enjoy yourself!

12:06.210 --> 12:07.040
Fine.

12:08.040 --> 12:09.670
Give me your best shot.

12:19.630 --> 12:20.470
Alright!

12:26.550 --> 12:28.422
"Monday, October 27 -
Unlucky Morning and Afternoon"

12:28.430 --> 12:31.512
"Tuesday, October 28 - Very Unlucky"

12:31.520 --> 12:34.382
"Wedesday, October 29 - Very Lucky"

12:34.390 --> 12:37.432
"Thursday, October 30 - Unlucky Midday"

12:37.440 --> 12:40.432
"Friday, October 31 - Lucky Morning"

12:40.440 --> 12:43.432
"Saturday, November 1 -
Lucky Morning and Evening"

12:43.440 --> 12:46.442
"Sunday, November 2 -
Unlucky Morning and Afternoon"

12:46.450 --> 12:49.192
"Monday, November 3 - Very Unlucky"

12:49.200 --> 12:51.030
"School Festival!!"
"Tuesday, November 4 - Very Lucky"

12:57.140 --> 12:59.080
E-Excuse us!

13:06.520 --> 13:07.960
-Sorry...
-Sorry we're late...

13:08.600 --> 13:10.470
What's with the getup?

13:11.150 --> 13:14.720
Our class is running a haunted cafe.

13:15.000 --> 13:17.392
Should've gone with something cuter.

13:17.400 --> 13:20.100
I had a heart attack.
You could've changed before coming!

13:20.370 --> 13:24.520
Sorry. We were both
on duty until the last minute.

13:25.020 --> 13:27.642
There's still others ahead of us.

13:27.650 --> 13:30.110
Take your time to change
and get that makeup off.

13:31.550 --> 13:33.642
Guess even you're afraid of ghosts?

13:33.650 --> 13:36.372
Not really... but I do get scared.

13:36.380 --> 13:37.642
Uh-huh.

13:37.650 --> 13:42.240
Here I thought never showing up for group
practice at all was a sign of fearlessness.

13:43.660 --> 13:46.582
I mean, it was you who said
solo practice wasn't enough

13:46.590 --> 13:49.900
and made me show up for club
practice daily before the break.

13:50.320 --> 13:53.830
It's precisely because I was
afraid that I didn't show.

13:57.500 --> 13:58.592
Oh, right.

13:58.600 --> 13:59.862
What?

13:59.870 --> 14:02.882
It was my fault, not yours.

14:02.890 --> 14:03.952
Eh?

14:03.960 --> 14:06.640
Oh, maybe some of it. Like, 9:1.

14:07.110 --> 14:09.282
Or maybe 7:3?

14:09.290 --> 14:10.012
Huh?

14:10.020 --> 14:13.270
Point is, I won't make you
feel that way again.

14:15.090 --> 14:19.592
Mayumori-san, I'd like you
to trust us once more.

14:19.600 --> 14:23.440
Musubu-chan, let Ururu-chan and
Kuma-chan fully dictate the rhythm.

14:23.880 --> 14:26.402
Do you get what you're saying?

14:26.410 --> 14:27.410
We do.

14:32.010 --> 14:33.450
Looks like we're next.

14:33.900 --> 14:35.790
Hands together, everyone.

14:36.040 --> 14:37.000
Musubu-chan.

14:37.740 --> 14:38.750
Omusubi.

14:43.260 --> 14:44.842
You do the honors, Uta-chan.

14:44.850 --> 14:46.532
Huh, why me?

14:46.540 --> 14:49.712
Because I feel like hearing from you.

14:49.720 --> 14:51.142
-Feel like?
-What a coincidence.

14:51.150 --> 14:52.752
I feel the same way.

14:52.760 --> 14:55.660
Wha... Er...

15:00.390 --> 15:05.062
A capella is about everyone
holding hands together in song.

15:05.070 --> 15:06.310
That's a great saying.

15:06.840 --> 15:11.402
Oh, um, that's
the president's words, not mine.

15:11.410 --> 15:16.242
I passed off someone else's
words as though they were mine...

15:16.250 --> 15:18.010
This is going nowhere.

15:19.720 --> 15:25.080
I'd like our hands to remain
connected throughout our song.

15:34.610 --> 15:37.112
That was the pop music club.

15:37.120 --> 15:39.950
Thanks for the wonderful show!

15:44.050 --> 15:45.572
Don't you think she's changed?

15:45.580 --> 15:47.030
Uta, and everyone else.

15:47.940 --> 15:49.522
I suppose so.

15:49.530 --> 15:51.180
Look forward to it.

15:51.720 --> 15:53.060
For what?

15:53.820 --> 15:56.060
I'm gonna be just a little bit serious.

15:57.590 --> 16:00.742
Last up are the girls of the a cappella club!

16:00.750 --> 16:02.170
It's time. Let's go.

16:25.500 --> 16:31.962
Girls have a secret button for love

16:31.970 --> 16:35.352
I won't lose this summer

16:35.360 --> 16:38.712
I'm not the weak girl I was

16:38.720 --> 16:44.420
Ah, my heart's all flustered

16:44.900 --> 16:48.972
In truth, anyone can fall in love

16:48.980 --> 16:51.472
Have courage and shine on

16:51.480 --> 16:55.602
In truth, romance is all about the timing

16:55.610 --> 17:00.990
Don't let it slip by

17:01.990 --> 17:05.242
Summer festival, our hands join

17:05.250 --> 17:08.362
As we watch the fireworks

17:08.370 --> 17:15.162
You call them beautiful while looking my way

17:15.170 --> 17:18.412
Dressed to impress, we scoop for goldfish

17:18.420 --> 17:21.672
You came out with three in the bag

17:21.680 --> 17:28.310
That's the kind of love
I dreamed at sweet fifteen

17:37.400 --> 17:38.610
Musubu-chan.

18:01.960 --> 18:07.432
Watching you from behind
as you ran across the field

18:07.440 --> 18:12.462
You looked so free,
even more than the clouds in the sky

18:12.470 --> 18:17.802
Even the squarish letters
you wrote in your notebook

18:17.810 --> 18:22.232
Seemed to me like a light
that lit up the whole world

18:22.240 --> 18:24.682
Seemed to me like a light

18:24.690 --> 18:30.012
I didn't know how it felt to be in love

18:30.020 --> 18:34.492
You'll never get another
chance to live this moment

18:34.500 --> 18:41.720
You're the one who taught me
what the words really meant

18:44.290 --> 18:46.932
I'll take these days I spent with you

18:46.940 --> 18:49.602
And etch them deep in my heart

18:49.610 --> 18:54.792
So even when I don't remember,
they'll still be safe inside me

18:54.800 --> 19:00.012
Even if one day I do
fall in love with someone else

19:00.020 --> 19:08.592
You'll still always be
so special, so precious

19:08.600 --> 19:15.350
As once again this season passes on by

19:37.320 --> 19:38.312
We did it!

19:38.320 --> 19:41.322
The rhythm was shaky,
everyone did their own thing,

19:41.330 --> 19:43.090
and the percussion ran solely on vibes.

19:43.810 --> 19:45.770
But it was fun, wasn't it?

19:52.270 --> 19:54.390
Thank you very much!

19:55.200 --> 19:56.020
Uta.

19:57.080 --> 19:59.520
I understand what you've been getting at.

20:02.090 --> 20:05.030
A cappella... is like a mille-feuille.

20:08.590 --> 20:09.500
Yeah...

20:18.620 --> 20:20.852
You must've practiced a ton.

20:20.860 --> 20:22.562
Yup, sure did.

20:22.570 --> 20:23.670
Thought so.

20:24.090 --> 20:26.032
We got good, huh?

20:26.040 --> 20:27.202
So-so.

20:27.210 --> 20:28.510
Harsh.

20:29.230 --> 20:30.962
You got through to me, though.

20:30.970 --> 20:35.130
I finally understood after letting myself
be swept by the band's harmony.

20:36.810 --> 20:38.300
I also saw your good side.

20:39.130 --> 20:42.852
You constantly use
your voice to tune the others.

20:42.860 --> 20:46.772
You observe everyone's actions
and attempt to understand us.

20:46.780 --> 20:48.100
I'm not worthy.

20:48.520 --> 20:50.600
Uta, you're a great fit for a cappella.

20:53.330 --> 20:56.910
I'll perform on stages at a higher
level than this in the future.

20:57.650 --> 21:00.790
I doubt a cappella will be the path I choose.

21:01.300 --> 21:02.530
I can see that.

21:02.840 --> 21:07.070
Despite that, I don't consider
today's performance a waste of time.

21:07.780 --> 21:09.920
This is something I'll look back to.

21:11.370 --> 21:13.960
I'm proud of you all...

21:14.570 --> 21:17.750
Correction, I'm proud of us.

21:25.050 --> 21:30.322
You know, our thoughts
and goals are nothing alike,

21:30.330 --> 21:32.740
but I learned that it's fine
to keep it that way.

21:33.470 --> 21:37.192
Still, it can't hurt to be on
the same page during a cappella.

21:37.200 --> 21:38.310
Yeah.

21:38.990 --> 21:41.870
This is why I love a cappella.

21:43.240 --> 21:46.792
You were amazing, Musubu-chan.
You've improved.

21:46.800 --> 21:47.730
Really?

21:48.090 --> 21:51.702
Yup. Now that I'm somewhat good at this,

21:51.710 --> 21:54.500
I've come to tell what makes you special.

21:55.390 --> 21:57.472
You're pretty much a beast.

21:57.480 --> 21:58.922
There's your bus.

21:58.930 --> 22:00.712
Yet you never took notice?

22:00.720 --> 22:01.330
Huh?

22:01.760 --> 22:05.290
There's a greater beast than I am.

22:07.550 --> 22:08.280
See you.

22:08.780 --> 22:10.330
Oh, see you.

22:14.180 --> 22:15.520
Which beast?

22:16.310 --> 22:18.740
Reirei, what was with today?

22:20.510 --> 22:22.152
Were you always this good?

22:22.160 --> 22:25.720
Have you been hiding it this whole time?!

22:26.270 --> 22:27.122
Yeah.

22:27.130 --> 22:28.422
Why?

22:28.430 --> 22:31.740
Because I wanted to keep
singing a cappella with you.

22:32.970 --> 22:35.060
And we will, forever.

22:37.590 --> 22:40.820
Airi, I'm joining Parabola.

22:41.160 --> 22:41.910
Eh?

22:43.960 --> 22:48.660
Honestly, you could've waited
until she finished high school.

22:49.070 --> 22:52.772
Nope, Parabola's at its peak
with our current members.

22:52.780 --> 22:55.612
I want us to be active
at our best as soon as possible.

22:55.620 --> 22:57.450
That so?

22:58.330 --> 23:02.130
Would've been nice for her
to finish her club on a positive note.

23:02.980 --> 23:05.880
Everyone says they love a cappella...

23:06.400 --> 23:09.090
Yet most students give up on it after school.

23:09.480 --> 23:11.212
What's this about?

23:11.220 --> 23:14.550
A cappella doesn't exactly
put food on the table.

23:14.820 --> 23:19.172
I can't stand a cappella being
confined to memories of one's youth.

23:19.180 --> 23:20.770
I'll change that.

23:21.900 --> 23:27.452
Our movement will make a cappella
a regular part of everyday life.

23:27.460 --> 23:30.422
To do that, we have to reach the top.

23:30.430 --> 23:32.730
Certain sacrifices are necessary.

23:34.900 --> 23:38.070
You're such a romantic, Mizuki-san.
